---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../config';
---

<Base title="Changelog" description="Release history and version notes for Flux AIO.">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <a href={url('/')}>Home</a> / <a href={url('/changelog')}>Changelog</a>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <h1>Changelog</h1>
      <p class="section-sub">Release history and version notes.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.20.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>

      <h3>Hunter &mdash; Threat Management</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Threat throttle</strong> &mdash; Opt-in threat management measured against whoever is actually tanking (a group tank <em>or</em> your pet, so it works solo). Above a threshold it Feigns Death on cooldown to keep threat low, and if Feign is down near the pull it drops to Auto Shot only rather than pulling. Off by default; a no-op on servers with no threat API.</li>
        <li><strong>Weave-Safe melee cap</strong> &mdash; Aggro pulls at roughly 110% of the tank&rsquo;s threat in melee versus ~130% at range, so sitting &ldquo;safe&rdquo; at range can one-shot you the instant you step in to Raptor weave. Weave-Safe holds you under the melee pull point at all times, with a configurable Melee Safety Cap.</li>
        <li><strong>Feign Death before Readiness</strong> &mdash; Optionally Feign right before Readiness fires: Readiness resets Feign so it costs you nothing, and your post-Readiness burst climbs from a clean threat slate.</li>
        <li><strong>Faster emergency Feign</strong> &mdash; Feign Death is off the global cooldown, so the auto-Feign now fires the instant aggro flips instead of waiting out the GCD after a shot.</li>
        <li><strong>Threat readout &amp; standalone HUD</strong> &mdash; Adds live threat lines to the combat dashboard (scaled %, raw %, Feign cooldown, throttle mode), plus an optional large movable Threat HUD colour-coded by how close you are to pulling. Both off by default.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.19.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>

      <h3>Paladin &mdash; Holy (rebuilt)</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>HealingEngine-driven targeting</strong> &mdash; Holy now heals whoever the HealingEngine surfaces (via a prediction hook), instead of a hand-rolled scan &mdash; so it reacts to incoming damage, absorbs and threat like the engine does.</li>
        <li><strong>Holy Light / Flash of Light selection with downranking</strong> &mdash; Picks Holy Light for real hits (or Divine Favor / Mortal-Strike targets) and the cheaper Flash of Light for light topping, then downranks to the rank that fits the wound &mdash; matching the top holy-paladin parses.</li>
        <li><strong>Mana conserve mode</strong> &mdash; Below a configurable mana floor it flips from Holy Light to efficient Flash of Light, so mana hovers at the floor instead of bottoming out on long fights.</li>
        <li><strong>Light&rsquo;s Grace weave</strong> &mdash; In a safe window with healthy mana, weaves a cheap Holy Light to keep the &minus;0.5s cast-time buff warm for your next real cast (toggleable).</li>
        <li><strong>Cancel wasted heals</strong> &mdash; Stops a mid-cast Holy Light / Flash of Light if the target died or the engine moved to a better one, and re-fires on the right unit.</li>
        <li><strong>Healing Assignment filter</strong> &mdash; Checkboxes to restrict healing/cleansing to Tanks / Self / Healers / DPS &mdash; uncheck the rest for a tank-only assignment.</li>
        <li><strong>Removed Holy Shock</strong> from the rotation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Paladin &mdash; Protection</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Fixed Righteous Defense taunt</strong> &mdash; It now scans for an elite/boss loose on an ally and taunts it off them, independent of your current target (the old logic stalled whenever you were already targeting the mob on you). Adds on a healer are taunted first.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Paladin &mdash; General</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Aura selector</strong> &mdash; Choose which aura to keep up (Auto by spec, or a specific one).</li>
        <li><strong>Auto Self-Blessing toggle</strong> &mdash; Turn off self-blessing in raids where Pally Power (or another paladin) manages your blessings.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Priest &mdash; Holy &amp; Discipline (rebuilt)</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>HealingEngine-driven targeting</strong> &mdash; Both healing specs now heal the engine&rsquo;s chosen target (with a prediction hook that surfaces shield / HoT / dispel targets), replacing the duplicate custom scanner.</li>
        <li><strong>Log-informed spell priority</strong> &mdash; Flash Heal is the primary heal (downranked to fit), Greater Heal fires only when free (Inner Focus / Holy Concentration), with Renew, Circle of Healing and Prayer of Mending doing the heavy lifting &mdash; mirroring the #1 holy-priest parses.</li>
        <li><strong>Mana conserve mode</strong> &mdash; A sliding Flash-Heal threshold that stops topping people off when mana runs low (Discipline drops hard-cast Greater Heal).</li>
        <li><strong>Dispel</strong> &mdash; Optional Dispel Magic / Abolish Disease on afflicted party members.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.18.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>

      <h3>Hunter &mdash; Melee Weave Coach</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Redesigned Weave HUD</strong> &mdash; A centered fill bar with range zones, a swing-aware STEP IN light, and a Raptor cooldown countdown, so the weave window reads at a glance.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed Weave Timing</strong> &mdash; The coach now reserves room for your full step-in and step-out before it lights up, and warns you to back out a true walk-out's worth of time before your next Auto Shot &mdash; instead of telling you to leave too late and clipping the shot. Weave timing also no longer shifts with your exact range.</li>
        <li><strong>Manual Melee Control</strong> &mdash; Optionally start your melee swing the instant you enter melee (for setups with WoW's Auto Attack / Auto Shot swap turned off), so an on-next-swing Raptor Strike always has a white hit to land on.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Hunter &mdash; Ranged</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Kill Command Fires Immediately</strong> &mdash; Kill Command is off the global cooldown, so it now goes the instant it's ready instead of being held for a GCD it never shared.</li>
        <li><strong>Readiness Pairs With Rapid Fire</strong> &mdash; Readiness now lines up with your second Rapid Fire (firing once the first has dropped) instead of being spent early in the opener.</li>
        <li><strong>v1 Keybind Workarounds</strong> &mdash; Under the v1 framework, the rotation paints stable, bindable icons for abilities the key-sender can't bind natively &mdash; Readiness and the Haste Potion &mdash; so you can finally key them.</li>
        <li><strong>Explosive Trap No Longer Auto-Drops in Melee</strong> &mdash; Its fire was breaking your own crowd control; queue it manually instead.</li>
        <li><strong>Tuned Defaults</strong> &mdash; A fresh profile now starts with the dialed-in weave timing, adaptive cast pad, and other PvE-safe settings.</li>
        <li><strong>New Hunter User Guide</strong> &mdash; A Hunter-focused guide (rotation, settings, the overlays, v1 binding, and the weave macro) added under <code>docs/</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Burst Cooldowns Fire on &ldquo;In Combat&rdquo;</strong> &mdash; Selecting &ldquo;In Combat&rdquo; on the Flux general tab now correctly triggers offensive cooldowns; they were previously ignored by the Hunter rotation logic.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.17.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>

      <h3>Paladin &mdash; Retribution</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Selectable Opener Judgement</strong> &mdash; The pull-time opener is now a dropdown (Off / Crusader / Wisdom / Light) instead of Crusader-only. Because Crusader Strike refreshes <em>all</em> Judgements on the target, a single pull application stays up the whole fight &mdash; so you can seed Judgement of Wisdom (raid mana) or Light (raid healing) just as easily as Crusader (+3% raid crit). Defaults to Crusader.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Paladin &mdash; All Specs</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Auto Freedom</strong> &mdash; New utility toggle (off by default) that self-casts Blessing of Freedom the moment you&rsquo;re rooted or snared, clearing the movement-impairing effect. Works in every spec. Note: Blessing of Freedom only removes roots and snares &mdash; it does not break stuns, fears, or polymorph.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.16.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>

      <h3>Paladin &mdash; Retribution</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Configurable Twist Lead</strong> &mdash; New <em>Twist Lead</em> slider (Retribution &gt; Seal Twisting, default 0.40s, range 0.25&ndash;0.80s) controls how early before your swing the rotation twists into Seal of Blood. Raise it to compensate for latency &mdash; the whole Command-prep &rarr; twist sequence shifts earlier together.</li>
        <li><strong>Crusader Strike No Longer Clips the Twist</strong> &mdash; Once Seal of Command was prepped, Crusader Strike and fillers (Hammer of Wrath, Exorcism, Consecration, Holy Wrath) could still fire in the ~1s before the swing, running their GCD into the twist window so the swing procced Command instead of twisting into Blood. They now hold once a twist is committed and only fire while Blood is the resident seal, sharply increasing twist count.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.15.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>

      <h3>Hunter &mdash; Ranged</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Adaptive DPS Engine</strong> &mdash; The ranged rotation is now a single per-tick engine that weighs every shot by its damage-per-cast and rebalances automatically as your haste changes, replacing the old fixed weave modes. Stings keep their pre-priority, and when no special beats waiting it simply lets Auto Shot ride.</li>
        <li><strong>Wing Clip Breaks Kael'thas Mind Control</strong> &mdash; With Infinity Blade equipped, targeting a Mind-Controlled ally now suggests only Wing Clip to break the control with melee damage, suppressing the rest of the rotation until they're free.</li>
        <li><strong>Sharper Immunity &amp; Enrage Handling</strong> &mdash; PvP immunities now follow the framework's maintained categories, PvE immunity is matched by spell ID (fixing a name collision that wrongly held DPS on Kael'thas), and Tranquilizing Shot reliably strips creature enrages. Feign Death also skips the Netherstrand Longbow.</li>
        <li><strong>Manual Raptor Queue</strong> &mdash; New <code>/flux raptor</code> command forces a single Raptor Strike weave window on demand for melee-weaving hunters.</li>
        <li><strong>Healthstone Actually Fires</strong> &mdash; The recovery middleware was registering the Master Healthstone as a spell instead of a bag item, so it never used it; corrected to match every other class.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.14.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>

      <h3>Build &amp; Display System</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Managed Multi-Group Display Scaffold</strong> &mdash; The TMW profile template moved from a single icon group to a managed multi-group layout (Shown Main / Hidden APL / Visible APL). This is shared display plumbing every class builds on, so a rotation can expose a hidden action-priority group plus a toggle-gated visible display without each class hand-maintaining its own group structure.</li>
        <li><strong>Scaffold Refreshes on Every Sync</strong> &mdash; The build now refreshes the managed group structure (groups, group count, texture) into existing profiles on every sync, not just on first creation, so older profiles upgrade to the new layout automatically. Note: this means in-game manual tweaks to group scale/columns/position are overwritten on the next sync &mdash; the group layout is build-managed.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.13.2 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>

      <h3>Warrior &mdash; Protection</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Thunder Clap Stays in Defensive Stance</strong> &mdash; The Prot rotation was dancing to Battle Stance every time it refreshed Thunder Clap, then swapping back &mdash; an unnecessary stance flicker mid-tanking. In TBC, Thunder Clap is castable in Defensive Stance, so it now fires in place with no stance swap.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.13.1 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>

      <h3>Paladin &mdash; Retribution</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Correct Twist Direction</strong> &mdash; TBC seal twisting is one-way: you can only twist <em>from</em> Seal of Command <em>into</em> Seal of Blood / Seal of the Martyr. v1.13.0 had it backwards (flashing Command in while Blood was resident, which doesn't twist). Now Blood/Martyr is the resident seal that rides through Crusader Strike, fillers and Judgement, and Seal of Command is briefly prepped before each swing so you twist into Blood &mdash; matching how a strong ret parses (Martyr-dominant uptime).</li>
        <li><strong>Smarter Judgement Timing</strong> &mdash; Judgement of Blood is now cast right before prepping Command for the twist, instead of mid-cycle. Since Judgement consumes the seal, the old timing forced an extra Seal of Blood re-cast that could clip the next twist; judging at the prep point uses up the seal you were about to drop anyway.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.13.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>

      <h3>Paladin &mdash; Retribution</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Seal Twist Inverted &mdash; Martyr Stays Up</strong> &mdash; The rotation kept Seal of Command as the resident seal and only flashed Seal of Blood / Seal of the Martyr in for the twist, so it kept falling back to Command after every Judgement. That inverted the seal uptimes versus a strong ret (Command-heavy instead of Martyr-heavy) and cost a lot of damage. Now Blood/Martyr is the resident seal &mdash; the guaranteed-damage seal you also Judge &mdash; and Seal of Command is briefly twisted in before each swing, then dropped back to Martyr.</li>
        <li><strong>Twist Seal Rank</strong> &mdash; New <code>ret_twist_seal_rank</code> dropdown (default Rank 1). The twisted-in Seal of Command was casting at max rank (280 mana) instead of Rank 1 (65 mana) because the rank wasn't forced &mdash; a steady mana drain. Rank 1 is recommended: the proc damage is identical at every rank.</li>
        <li><strong>Crusader Strike On Cooldown</strong> &mdash; Crusader Strike was firing every ~9-11s instead of on its 6s cooldown, because it was blocked for the entire last ~1.5s of every swing. It now only yields during the 0.4s twist window and fires near its cooldown.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.12.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>

      <h3>Paladin &mdash; Retribution</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Seal Twisting Fixed</strong> &mdash; The swing timer was misread (<code>GetSwing</code> returns time <em>remaining</em>, not swing duration), which opened the twist window near the swing's midpoint &mdash; about 1.8s too early. Seal of Blood / Seal of the Martyr was cast far too soon and overwritten before the swing landed, so it procced on only a fraction of hits (~18 vs ~113 in a clean log) while wasting mana on re-seals. The twist now fires in the correct final-0.4s window, sustaining the seal across swings.</li>
        <li><strong>Heart of the Crusader Opener</strong> &mdash; New <code>ret_opener_crusader</code> toggle (on by default). On the pull, casts Seal of the Crusader and Judges it to apply the +3% raid crit debuff; Crusader Strike refreshes it for the rest of the fight. Skips automatically if another paladin already has the debuff up, and won't get stuck if Judgement is on cooldown.</li>
        <li><strong>Avenging Wrath Modes</strong> &mdash; New <code>ret_avenging_wrath</code> dropdown: <code>Never</code>, <code>On Cooldown</code>, <code>On Bosses</code>, or <code>During Burst</code> (default). No longer fires automatically on cooldown &mdash; it now waits for a burst trigger by default. Protection's Avenging Wrath is unchanged.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.11.1 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>

      <h3>Shaman &mdash; Enhancement</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Twist Cycles Now Self-Correct</strong> &mdash; The Windfury / Grace of Air and Fire Nova / Magma twist state machines tracked recommended drops rather than actual ones. If a recommendation window was missed (rotation icon shown but macro not pressed in time), the cycle desynced &mdash; symptoms included back-to-back Windfury drops with no Grace between and ~30s gaps with nothing dropping. Both twists now read <code>GetTotemInfo</code> each frame and act on what's actually deployed, so a missed window is recovered on the next frame automatically.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.11.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>

      <h3>Shaman &mdash; Enhancement</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Swing Sync Detection</strong> &mdash; CLEU-based MH/OH tracker that reports stagger state on the combat dashboard (<code>OH lead</code> / <code>OK</code> / <code>Drift</code>). Helps you stay inside Flurry's 0.5s shared-charge window.</li>
        <li><strong>Auto Swing Resync (opt-in)</strong> &mdash; Optional auto-fire of the resync macro (<code>/cleartarget</code> + <code>/targetlasttarget</code> + <code>/startattack</code>) when stagger drifts outside the Flurry window. Hysteresis dead-zone and swing-midpoint gating to avoid no-op fires. Off by default; most players will prefer to watch the dashboard and press manually.</li>
        <li><strong>WF / Grace Twist Rate Fix</strong> &mdash; Twist phases were both holding for <code>CYCLE_TIME = 10s</code>, producing a 20s full loop instead of ~10s &mdash; roughly half the rate intended. Replaced with phase-specific durations (WF 1.5s, Grace 7.5s) so WF re-drops just before the carried 10s buff expires.</li>
        <li><strong>Post-FNT Fire Totem Dropdown</strong> &mdash; New <code>enh_fnt_post_totem</code> setting (default Magma) controls the totem dropped between Fire Nova explosions. Lets you keep Nova → Magma → Nova cadence without forcing Magma as the single-target default.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Shaman &mdash; Elemental / Enhancement</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Hold Shocks (Interrupts Only)</strong> &mdash; New <code>ele_shock_interrupt_only</code> / <code>enh_shock_interrupt_only</code> toggles suppress rotation shocks so the interrupt middleware can reserve them for kicks. Useful in dungeons.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Shaman &mdash; All Specs</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Grounding &amp; Tremor Totems</strong> &mdash; Now selectable as the default air / earth totem on every spec. Auto-Tremor middleware behavior unchanged.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.10.1 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>

      <h3>Warrior</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Explicit Click Targeting</strong> &mdash; Bloodthirst, Execute, and Victory Rush now ship with explicit <code>Click.autounit = "harm"</code> so they don't fall back to the framework's "both" auto-detect on TBC clients with incomplete <code>IsHarmfulSpell</code> metadata. Eliminates spurious "Target is not valid" errors during target transitions.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.10.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>

      <h3>Druid &mdash; Cat</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Target Focus Behind Check</strong> &mdash; New General toggle that treats "behind" as "target isn't targeting me" (`targettarget ~= player`) instead of the geometric position check. Useful in groups where the tank holds threat.</li>
        <li><strong>Powershift &amp; Tick Optimization</strong> &mdash; Powershift logic and energy-tick tracking aligned to wowsims TBC feral sim. New <code>Shift Delay Window</code> slider (0.5&ndash;1.5s, step 0.05).</li>
        <li><strong>Mangle Trick Wired Up</strong> &mdash; The <code>use_mangle_trick</code> setting is now actually read by the code (previously dead). Includes the sim's skip clause: skipped when Rake Trick is on and Mangle isn't fully discounted by 2pT6. Also gated on Mangle being off cooldown so it doesn't block Shred while waiting on Mangle CD.</li>
        <li><strong>Bite-Aware Shift Delay</strong> &mdash; The "is a tick worth waiting for?" calculation now counts regular Ferocious Bite as a valid next action at max CP (energy 15&ndash;19 + 5 CP correctly delays the shift since the tick lands at 35&ndash;39, Bite-eligible).</li>
        <li><strong>WolfsheadShred Restored</strong> &mdash; Position-agnostic Wolfshead powershift back in the priority list; respects the <code>!rip_next</code> gate to avoid burning a shift when a tick will reach Rip cost.</li>
        <li><strong>/fticks Default Off</strong> &mdash; Energy-tick debug printing no longer spams chat on load. Toggle on with <code>/fticks</code>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Druid &mdash; Balance</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Arcane-Immune Handling</strong> &mdash; Skip Starfire/Moonfire vs arcane-immune targets, route to Wrath/Insect Swarm. Shared <code>NS.ARCANE_IMMUNE</code> table in core.</li>
        <li><strong>Starfire Downranking</strong> &mdash; Auto-downrank Starfire to rank 6 in mana-conservation tier (mirrors wowsims).</li>
        <li><strong>Insect Swarm Target Filter</strong> &mdash; Always-on with target classification dropdown (all/elites+/bosses/off). 4p T5 (Nordrassil Regalia) forces IS at lowest mana tier.</li>
        <li><strong>Caster Stance Guard</strong> &mdash; Emergency/proactive heals and dispels now gated on caster stance so they don't fire in Bear/Cat/Moonkin.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>UI / Settings</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Fractional Slider Step Fix</strong> &mdash; Settings sliders with non-integer <code>step</code> now snap to multiples of step instead of rounding to nearest integer.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.9.1 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-fix">Fix</span>

      <h3>Druid</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Smart Shift Delay Tuning</strong> &mdash; Reduced delay threshold from 1.0s to 0.725s for tighter powershift timing.</li>
        <li><strong>Bite Trick CP Gate</strong> &mdash; Bite trick now respects the FB Min Combo Points setting instead of a hardcoded 3 CP minimum.</li>
        <li><strong>Shift Delay CP Awareness</strong> &mdash; Smart shift delay no longer stalls waiting for bite energy when you don't have enough combo points to bite. Rake trick correctly uses its own energy cost without a CP check.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section changelog-entry">
      <h2>v1.9.0 <span class="changelog-date">2026</span></h2>
      <span class="changelog-tag tag-feature">Feature</span>

      <h3>Warrior</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Arms &amp; Fury DPS Improvements</strong> &mdash; Revised rotation priorities for higher sustained damage output.</li>
        <li><strong>Kebab Spec</strong> &mdash; New warrior playstyle option.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Paladin</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Holy Healing Overhaul</strong> &mdash; Reworked healing rotation with intelligent spell selection and downranking.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Priest</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Shadow Rotation Improvements</strong> &mdash; Revised shadow priority logic for better DPS output.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Druid</h3>
      <ul class="features">
        <li><strong>Resto Downranking</strong> &mdash; Healing spells now correctly downrank based on HP deficit and mana efficiency.</li>
        <li><strong>Smarter Swipe AoE Threshold</strong> &mdash; The +1 elite bump now only applies when elites are a minority in the pack. Pure elite packs cleave at your configured threshold.</li>
        <li><strong>Tick Tracker Powershift Fix</strong> &mdash; Energy tick tracker now resets correctly on powershift instead of extrapolating from stale pre-shift timing.</li>
        <li><strong>Rip Min TTD Floor</strong> &mdash; Slider minimum lowered from 8 to 0, allowing the TTD gate to be fully disabled.</li>
      </ul>
